**Convention 109.3 (work, coexistence and precision).** General preparation
pays its actual forcing/control matrix construction and solve; marker
preparation pays target reception, $2k$ operand constructions and the
old-size Tick. Both pay constructor traversal and raw lifecycle updates,
source/code installation, exact arithmetic, authentic references/grants
and real clearing/isolation. Their four feedback Ticks are grown-size.
A size-$m$ unit-tree source Tick initializes $m$ update slots and uses
$2(m-1)$ directed neighbor additions; a maintained predictor pays its
own separate update and buffers. For the marker schedule there is one
size-$N$ preparation Tick and four size-$M$ receiver Ticks. General
preparation instead has $I$ size-$N$ Ticks. Repair and passive suffixes
have their displayed size-$M$ Ticks. Exact linear-combination formulas
for the known local sectors require finite work; selecting and solving
the $R$ complement, forming current fields, metrics, germs and exports
are additional paid computations. No spectral oracle is used.

One sufficient numerical receiver fills the size-$M$ field from the
disjoint local formulas in $O(M+k)$ rational operations after acquisition.
For partial-advice repair, ordinary elimination on $R$, followed by the
standard coordinate rows and the consistent augmented system, uses
$O((r+k)k^2)$ rational operations. Forming the advanced field then again
uses $O(M+k)$. A literal designated germ can be computed by $M-1$
sparse updates in $O(M^2)$ rational operations, in addition to its
$bM$-word export. A subsequent $n$-pair passive suffix costs $O(nM)$
predictor operations. These are sufficient numerical bounds, excluding
the separately counted structural navigation, codecs, copies and clears.
At maximum actual intermediate width $W$, multiply the arithmetic
counts by the selected exact rational-operation cost at width $W$.

For example, reserve separately $2M$ plant slots, $2M$ predictor/update
slots and $k$ acquired parameter slots. A sufficient late solve layout
adds $2rk+4k^2+8k+2r$ rational slots for copies of $R$, its elimination,
coordinate-complement and augmented work, retained advice and vectors.
The original general producer additionally uses the supplier's
$Nb(I+1)$ integer forcing-coefficient slots, $b(I+1)$ rational control
slots and its $N$-coordinate owned target. Its coefficient construction
and dense multiplication are those of NLBAII Proposition 65.2. The
marker producer uses its own target and operand buffers instead; it
does not inherit a free general-producer solve. These sufficient
reservations are not space minima. Any isolated preparation allocations
still present at the repair cut remain additional capacities, and every
literal exported germ, Time record or other copy needs its own backing.

Count simultaneous source old/new fields, full predictor old/new fields
when installed, graph and exhaustive bindings, reference/grant stores,
parser and pending request/reply bytes, owned targets and general control
blocks while live, the $k$ acquired rationals, control packets, literal
$R\theta$, solve scratch, counters, requested records and output copies,
and every inaccessible but still allocated provider capacity. Distinct
copies count separately and actual shared allocations once. Clearing
writes do not remove cleared backing from the resource vector. Requested
Time is an additional real record when retained; replacing one record
does not erase other exported copies.

All rational numerators/denominators and integer phase counters have
their actual widths. The input $\theta$ and preparation intermediates
have no dimension-only width bound. Finite program code and termination
per input imply neither constant memory nor uniform lifetime, finite-bit,
energy or physical resource bounds. The displayed calls are derived
schedule counts. No implementation, bit-traffic measurement, running-time
measurement, backing peak or engineering cost was obtained from them;
none of those unmeasured quantities is assigned zero.

